    },
    {
      "id": "VNK4pB2accJCejXhkqVmQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1341.033854166667,
      "y": -16.748697916666742,
      "width": 1181.2469075520826,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1139136363,
      "version": 255,
      "versionNonce": 1783601099,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788179515893,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Aven — a Java/Spring Boot microservices platform that models how a fintech's internal ledger works: every transaction\nis recorded as balanced double-entry bookkeeping (debits = credits, immutable, never edited), published reliably to Kafka\nvia the outbox pattern, asynchronously settled by a separate service, and independently verified by a reconciliation\nservice that replays the event log rather than trusting cached balances. \nFive services (ledger, account, settlement, reconciliation, api-gateway), each with its own Postgres DB, coordinated\nentirely through Kafka events — no service reaches into another's database.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Aven — a Java/Spring Boot microservices platform that models how a fintech's internal ledger works: every transaction is recorded as balanced double-entry bookkeeping (debits = credits, immutable, never edited), published reliably to Kafka via the outbox pattern, asynchronously settled by a separate service, and independently verified by a reconciliation service that replays the event log rather than trusting cached balances. \nFive services (ledger, account, settlement, reconciliation, api-gateway), each with its own Postgres DB, coordinated entirely through Kafka events — no service reaches into another's database.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uRFilbhX8gGx3RWGEUcYc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1657.8867187500005,
      "y": 161.63578869047603,
      "width": 879.9755859375,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1665260677,
      "version": 303,
      "versionNonce": 1740806757,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788179669626,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Ledger Service — records double-entry transactions (debit/credit pairs), enforces the\nbalanced-entry invariant, append-only (corrections via reversal, never edits). Writes to its\nown Postgres DB and publishes events via the outbox pattern. REST-driven.\nSettlement Service — batches pending transactions on a schedule, simulates async\nsettlement, retries failures with backoff, routes persistent failures to a dead-letter\ntopic. Kafka-driven (consumer) + scheduled job.\nReconciliation Service — independently replays the entire Kafka event log (its own\nconsumer group, from-earliest) to recompute balances from scratch, then compares\nagainst Account Service's cache and flags drift. This is the standout/\"wow\" service for\ninterviews. Kafka-driven (consumer).\nAPI Gateway — single entry point, routes external requests to the right service (Spring\nCloud Gateway). No DB of its own.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ledger Service — records double-entry transactions (debit/credit pairs), enforces the balanced-entry invariant, append-only (corrections via reversal, never edits). Writes to its own Postgres DB and publishes events via the outbox pattern. REST-driven.\nSettlement Service — batches pending transactions on a schedule, simulates async settlement, retries failures with backoff, routes persistent failures to a dead-letter topic. Kafka-driven (consumer) + scheduled job.\nReconciliation Service — independently replays the entire Kafka event log (its own consumer group, from-earliest) to recompute balances from scratch, then compares against Account Service's cache and flags drift. This is the standout/\"wow\" service for interviews. Kafka-driven (consumer).\nAPI Gateway — single entry point, routes external requests to the right service (Spring Cloud Gateway). No DB of its own.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
